 "notes": "The list starts on n41.jpg (p. 34) and finishes with three rows at the top of n42.jpg (p. 35). n40.jpg (p. 33) only has the section's introduction, so I didn't open n43.jpg.\n\n- Type is printed in small capitals (\"L.H.\", \"L.V.\"). I've written it in normal capitals.\n- Leader dots: the \"printed\" field gives them as rough runs of \"...\". Their exact number isn't meaningful.\n- No map numbers and no light characters are printed.\n- The † after Longstone L.H. points to a footnote at the foot of p. 34: \"† For nature of light, position, and distance from the nearest land, see Report for 1880.\" The † belongs only to the Longstone row.\n- Count: 37 rows, 25 of them starred, which matches \"returns have been received from twenty-five\" on p. 33. That page also says schedules went to \"thirty-seven lighthouses and light-vessels on the East Coast of England, and two stations in the Channel Islands\" (39 in all). The list has only 35 East Coast stations plus the two Channel Islands stations (Casquets and Hanois), so it is two short of the text's count.\n- The Channel Islands rows have no sub-heading of their own; they continue the East Coast list. On p. 35 \"EAST COAST OF ENGLAND.\" is just the page's running head.\n- Spellings copied as printed (the usual forms are in brackets): \"Llyn Wells\" (Lynn Well), \"Hasbro'\" (Happisburgh), \"Languard Point\" (Landguard Point), \"Orfordness\", \"Spurn (Newsand)\", \"Eastside\" (one word), \"Newarp\". \"C. Prefrement\" (Cockle L.V.) is an odd surname and may be misprinted, but it is clearly printed that way. \"Edward le Gallais\" has a lower-case \"le\".\n- OCR errors corrected from the image: \"Hastside\" is really \"*Eastside\". \"*South Sand\" is really \"*South Sand Head L.V.\". \"Spurn Giléwiend\" is really \"Spurn (Newsand) L.V.\". \"©. Campbell\" is really \"C. Campbell\".\n- Hasbro' L.H.: the observer column reads \"By Mr. Gurney from G. H. Dunsford.\" I put G. H. Dunsford in keepers as the observer. Mr. Gurney (J. H. Gurney, jun.) passed the return on and is not a keeper, so \"By Mr. Gurney from\" is in other.\n- Shipwash and Galloper: the observer is given only as \"The Principal\" (the light-vessel's master), not by name. I kept it in keepers as printed, but it is a post, not a person. Galloper's entry runs onto a second line: \"two batches of wings from Mr. Gurney.\" I joined it into one row.\n- Outer Dowsing: the type looks like \"L,V.\" in the scan, probably a broken full stop. I transcribed it as seen and flagged it.\n- Two pairs share a name: Hasbro' L.H. and Hasbro' L.V., and Spurn L.H. and Spurn (Newsand) L.V.\n- Keeper entries keep their final full stops as printed (e.g. \"Thomas O. Hall.\").",
